{"result": {"response": {"id": "chatcmpl-f0f0057e-798f-9605-953f-1950ff86bfcf", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Probiotic Drugs and Antimicrobial Interactions Community\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on a group of probiotic drugs—including 双歧杆菌四联活菌 (Bifidobacterium quadruple viable), 双歧杆菌三联活菌 (Bifidobacterium triple viable), 地衣芽孢杆菌活菌 (Bacillus licheniformis viable), 复合乳酸菌肠溶 (Compound Lactobacillus enteric-coated), 复方嗜酸乳杆菌 (Compound Acidophilus Lactobacillus), 整肠生 (Zheng Chang Sheng), 枯草杆菌二联活菌 (Bacillus subtilis double viable), 乳酸菌素 (Lactasin), and 小儿乳酸菌素 (Pediatric Lactasin)—that are primarily indicated for gastrointestinal conditions such as diarrhea, constipation, and gut flora imbalance. These drugs share significant interaction relationships with antimicrobial agents (抗菌药), adsorbents like 药用炭 (medicinal charcoal), and other drug classes such as 铋剂 (bismuth agents) and 酊剂 (tinctures), which can inhibit or kill the live bacteria in these formulations. The network also includes associated diseases (e.g., 急慢性腹泻, 内毒素血症) and side effects (e.g., 吸收减少).\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Core probiotic drugs target gut microbiota-related disorders\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Multiple probiotic drugs in this community are explicitly indicated for conditions stemming from gastrointestinal flora imbalance. For example, 双歧杆菌三联活菌 is indicated for acute and chronic diarrhea, constipation, mild-to-moderate acute diarrhea, indigestion, bloating, and as an adjunct treatment for endotoxemia caused by gut dysbiosis [Data: Relationships (20147, 20149, 20148, 20153)]. Similarly, 地衣芽孢杆菌活菌 is used for bacterial or fungal-induced acute/chronic enteritis and diarrhea, and for preventing/treating other forms of gut flora imbalance [Data: Relationships (20469, 20470)]. 乳酸菌素 treats pediatric diarrhea, abnormal intestinal fermentation, indigestion, and enteritis [Data: Relationships (19232, 19234)]. These indications highlight a shared therapeutic focus on restoring or supporting healthy gut microbiota to manage digestive symptoms and complications.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Widespread negative interactions with antimicrobial agents\",\n            \"explanation\": \"A critical finding is that nearly all probiotic drugs in this community exhibit documented negative interactions with 抗菌药 (antibacterial agents), which can reduce or nullify their efficacy. For instance, 复合乳酸菌肠溶, 复方嗜酸乳杆菌, and 整肠生 should not be co-administered with antibacterials; if necessary, dosing should be separated by at least three hours [Data: Relationships (34471, 34569, 38918)]. Additionally, 双歧杆菌三联活菌’s efficacy may be compromised by concurrent antibacterial use due to its live bacterial content. This pattern underscores a major clinical consideration: probiotics containing live microorganisms are pharmacologically incompatible with broad-spectrum antimicrobials unless carefully timed [Data: Entities (11018); Relationships (34471, 34569, 38918, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Adsorbent agents like medicinal charcoal impair probiotic function\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Several probiotic formulations are contraindicated with adsorbent agents, particularly 药用炭 (medicinal charcoal) and related compounds like 白陶土 (kaolin). Evidence shows that 药用炭 can adsorb or inhibit live bacteria in probiotics, rendering them ineffective. Specific interactions include those between 双歧杆菌四联活菌 and 药用碳 [Data: Relationships (32046)], 枯草杆菌二联活菌 and 药用炭 [Data: Relationships (39582)], 小儿乳酸菌素 and 药用炭 [Data: Relationships (36823)], and 消化酶类 and 药用炭 [Data: Relationships (50042)]. Furthermore, 药用炭 itself is associated with the adverse effect of 吸收减少 (reduced absorption) [Data: Relationships (15986)], reinforcing its role as a potent adsorbent that interferes with drug bioavailability. These findings indicate that adsorbents pose a significant risk to the therapeutic integrity of live microbial products.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Additional incompatibilities with bismuth agents and tinctures\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond antimicrobials and adsorbents, probiotic drugs are also incompatible with 铋剂 (bismuth preparations) and 酊剂 (tinctures). Structured evidence states that bismuth agents, tannic acid, activated charcoal, and tinctures can suppress, adsorb, or kill live enterococci, making co-administration inadvisable [Data: Relationships (27762, 27763)]. Although 铋剂 and 酊剂 appear less frequently in the dataset (degree 3 and 4, respectively), their inclusion in multiple interaction warnings highlights their recognized inhibitory effects on live bacterial therapeutics. This reinforces a broader class-level caution against combining probiotics with substances known to have antimicrobial or binding properties.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Overlap between probiotic indications and pediatric use\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Several entities in the community are specifically relevant to pediatric populations. For example, 乳酸菌素 and 小儿乳酸菌素 are indicated for 小儿腹泻 (pediatric diarrhea) [Data: Relationships (19232); Entities (757, 5162)]. Additionally, 双歧杆菌四联活菌 carries a contraindication note stating that children must use it under adult supervision [Data: Relationships (5861)], suggesting cautious pediatric application. This indicates that a subset of the probiotic drugs in this network are tailored or commonly used for childhood gastrointestinal issues, necessitating special dosing or monitoring considerations in younger patients.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Antibacterial drug class encompasses newer subclasses like 新喹诺酮类\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The 抗菌药 (antibacterial agents) category serves as a central interacting class in this community and includes more specific subclasses. Notably, 新喹诺酮类 (new quinolones) is classified under 抗菌药 [Data: Relationships (57222)], indicating that even advanced-generation antibiotics fall within the scope of agents that may interfere with probiotic efficacy. This hierarchical relationship confirms that the interaction warnings apply broadly across antibiotic types, not just older or narrow-spectrum agents, thereby increasing the clinical relevance of these contraindications in modern therapeutic contexts.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Side effects and secondary indications linked to adsorbents\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While primarily known for their interference with other drugs, adsorbents like 药用炭 also have therapeutic indications and adverse effects of their own. 药用炭 is indicated for 腹泻及胃肠胀气 (diarrhea and gastrointestinal bloating) [Data: Relationships (24481)], positioning it as both a treatment for some of the same conditions addressed by probiotics and a potential antagonist to their mechanism. Simultaneously, it is associated with 吸收减少 (reduced absorption) as an adverse reaction [Data: Relationships (15986)], illustrating its dual role as a symptomatic remedy and a source of pharmacokinetic interference. This duality complicates clinical decision-making when managing gastrointestinal disorders.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses moderate-to-high clinical impact due to widespread drug-drug incompatibilities that can significantly reduce treatment efficacy if not properly managed.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782128610, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1776, "prompt_tokens": 5632, "total_tokens": 7408, "completion_tokens_de